Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:06.640 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  hello and welcome back to the heroes  path  our journey to uncover the different  routes the key players took during the  event known as the great calamity this  is episode 3 of a seven-part mini-series  covering this subject  if you haven't watched the first two be  sure to give them a watch too as this  part  ties into the overall arc presented in  those episodes  today i'm joined by my good friend  conrad better known as the host of the  commonwealth realm  a wonderful channel devoted to  everything nintendo and in particular  the zelda franchise  let's just say that this isn't the first  time we have worked together  as we have been creating content  together for well over a year now and  i'm happy as always to have him with me  on the channel and continue this trend  and very fitting too since he is  apparently closest to the rook in terms  of his appearance  if we are to believe this app he too  will be posting his own video about the  upcoming hyrule warriors age of calamity  and how it will be the darkest zelda  game  up until the release of the highly  anticipated breath of the wild 2.  a link to his video will be in the  description and the end card as always  but enough delay let's jump right back  into the noise  the moment the return of the fabled  calamity gannon is undeniable  derek doesn't hesitate for a moment and  commands the pilots to get to the divine  beasts  as quickly as possible and urges link to  head for hyrule castle with the strategy  now set  the group moves across the promenade  when they reach the west gate of the  lanera road  princess zelda link and obosa continue  on to kakariko village  while the rook moves over quarters shelf  and down in the la neru wetlands  interestingly enough instead of sticking  to the east side of the wetlands and  heading for zoro river in a straight  line which would be faster he slightly  moves north west and crosses right  through kapunka village  the rook small detail suggests that he  might have purposely decided to drop by  gapunga village  either to warn the villagers or to  actually take part in a small battle  at this point it would be way too early  for any guardians to have arrived here  as  link and zelda are only barely halfway  to the castle however  age of calamity shows us that guardians  weren't the extent of the hylian's  problems  as we see both monsters and guardians  taking part in the war  gopunga village might be under siege by  a horde of monsters at this point  most likely lisafos as they are native  to this region  on top of that creating a champion shows  that an evacuation line for the citizens  of kapunka  was set up from the village up  sahasrara's slope  and into kakariko village it's possible  that daruk took the lead in this  evacuation instructing the villagers on  where to go  from gaponga village the rook treks  across lineback island  over the pier that stretches across the  zoro river and up into trilby valley  as he moves further up he reaches a fork  in the road one of which leads north  east across turner trail  and towards akala citadel or north into  the moor of death mountain and towards  goran city  and subsequently varudanya just like  what was the case with urbosa's path  age of calamity might choose to alter  the backstory provided by creating a  champion and come up with a slightly  different scenario  in the book the rook moves straight up  the maw of death mountain and to his  divine beast without any detours  however in the trailer for age of  calamity we see a short scene of daruk  battling a high knocks at akala citadel  what we don't know as of right now is if  this takes part before  or during the calamity daruk is wearing  his blue champion's cloth but as some  have pointed out the cloth was received  before the champion started their  training sessions to control their  divine beasts  so there could be enough time in between  for this to happen  on the other hand we can spot a  seemingly dead guardian in the  background  which shouldn't be there before the  calamity since all the guardians were  supposedly being kept at hyrule castle  this still leaves the option open for  this taking place during the calamity  rather than before it  in this case we're going to do the same  thing we did with urbosa and sketch a  gameplay scenario to cover both  options one in which guru plays part in  the defense of the citadel  and one in which he goes straight for  his divine beast if the part where deruk  fights at the citadel turns out to take  place before the calamity you can  consider this next scenario vane and  just skip straight to the part where  daruk moves up to death mountain  it is possible that age of calamity will  see us experience the battle for akala  citadel partly through the rook's eyes  at some point during the disaster an  evacuation line for civilians  and soldiers was set up from the east  gate of castletown  all the way to the citadel if the rook  spent a decent amount of time at gaponga  village this evacuation could be well  underway by the time he reaches the  crossroads between  tourneo trail and the maw of death  mountain this could provide a motivation  for the rook to go off course for a  while  feeling pressured to keep the desperate  civilians and soldiers safe from whoever  or whatever might be in pursuit of them  he escorts the hylians to the citadel  safely and briefly helps with the  defense until the soldiers have taken  their positions and can take over the  defense from there  it's unlikely that daruk will actually  go inside the citadel but rather  fight in front of it perhaps at the  akala bridge akala span or maybe even  the parade grounds below  getting to his divine beast is still the  highest priority  and actually going inside the walls of  the citadel would make no sense  since the front gate had to have been  sealed at some point to deny access to  the incoming guardian  hordes if we are to actually experience  the later stages of the battle for akala  citadel through gameplay  this will probably be through the eyes  of a different unspecified character  or it could even be only reserved for  cutscenes  with the battle of akala citadel about  to heat up the rook moves into the moor  of death mountain and a long climb up  the mountain road towards scotland city  there's a probability that this section  could be playable linear battle up the  mountain with monsters potentially  coming in from the front and guardians  in pursuit from behind  the maw of death mountain is absolutely  littered with dead guardians  and they can even be found further up  the road with some as far as beyond the  southern mine  we know that goron city itself was  ultimately spared from any  harm and the route might have a big role  in saving his hometown  fighting off the guardians coming in  from behind him as he made his way  up when the route finally reaches goron  city all that remains is a short hike  past the goron hot springs and across  the eldin bridge  there he unites with varadania on the  side of death mountain  he takes his divine beast into firing  position when suddenly an  unexpectedly calamity ganon unleashes  strands of malice aimed towards  mechanical beasts  with impeccable aim the machine that was  meant to subdue ganon  suddenly became a death trap for the  goron champion inside the walls of the  corrupted varidani  a spectre manifests itself from  seemingly nova  fireblad ganon with nowhere left to go  and determined to retake his ancient war  machine  the rook embroils himself into a fight  to the death with ganon's malice infused  phantom  one he is destined to lose as the blight  extinguishes his light  his spirit gets sealed inside the  mechanical monster  and becomes a mere ghost in the shell of  a machine that was supposed to bring  victory the death of the goron hero is  just one more of many tragedies still  awaiting us in age of calamity but his  sacrifice is never forgotten by his  people  and offspring won't be until 100 years  from now that link with the help of his  ancestor  yunovo will grant him an opportunity to  take a sweet revenge  on the malice infused monstrosity which  ended his life  [Music]  [Music]  you

